{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1868","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Fill in the Matrix"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is an empty matrix $$$M$$$ of size $$$n\\times m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Zhongkao examination is over, and Daniel would like to do some puzzle games. He is going to fill in the matrix $$$M$$$ using permutations of length $$$m$$$. That is, each row of $$$M$$$ must be a permutation of length $$$m^\\dagger$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Define the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the $$$i$$$-th column in $$$M$$$ as $$$v_i=\\operatorname{MEX}(M_{1,i},M_{2,i},\\ldots,M_{n,i})^\\ddagger$$$. Since Daniel likes diversity, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beauty"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$M$$$ is $$$s=\\operatorname{MEX}(v_1,v_2,\\cdots,v_m)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to help Daniel fill in the matrix $$$M$$$ and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"maximize"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" its beauty."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\dagger$$$ A permutation of length $$$m$$$ is an array consisting of $$$m$$$ distinct integers from $$$0$$$ to $$$m-1$$$ in arbitrary order. For example, $$$[1,2,0,4,3]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[0,1,1]$$$ is not a permutation ($$$1$$$ appears twice in the array), and $$$[0,1,3]$$$ is also not a permutation ($$$m-1=2$$$ but there is $$$3$$$ in the array)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\ddagger$$$ The $$$\\operatorname{MEX}$$$ of an array is the smallest non-negative integer that does not belong to the array. For example, $$$\\operatorname{MEX}(2,2,1)=0$$$ because $$$0$$$ does not belong to the array, and $$$\\operatorname{MEX}(0,3,1,2)=4$$$ because $$$0$$$, $$$1$$$, $$$2$$$ and $$$3$$$ appear in the array, but $$$4$$$ does not."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\le t\\le 1000$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1\\le n,m\\le 2\\cdot 10^5$$$) — the size of the matrix."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n\\cdot m$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, in the first line output a single integer — the maximum beauty of $$$M$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then output the matrix $$$M$$$ of size $$$n\\times m$$$ — the matrix you find."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple solutions, you may output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n4 3\n1 16\n6 6\n2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 0 2\n0 2 1\n1 0 2\n0 2 1\n2\n14 7 15 4 10 0 8 6 1 2 3 5 9 11 12 13 \n6\n3 0 1 4 2 5 \n5 2 1 0 4 3 \n1 3 2 4 5 0 \n4 1 3 2 5 0 \n4 2 5 3 0 1 \n2 4 0 5 1 3\n0\n0\n0"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_1=\\operatorname{MEX}(1,0,1,0)=2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_2=\\operatorname{MEX}(0,2,0,2)=1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_3=\\operatorname{MEX}(2,1,2,1)=0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Therefore, $$$s=\\operatorname{MEX}(2,1,0)=3$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be shown that $$$3$$$ is the maximum possible beauty of $$$M$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, any permutation will make $$$s=2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_1=\\operatorname{MEX}(3,5,1,4,4,2)=0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_2=\\operatorname{MEX}(0,2,3,1,2,4)=5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_3=\\operatorname{MEX}(1,1,2,3,5,0)=4$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_4=\\operatorname{MEX}(4,0,4,2,3,5)=1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_5=\\operatorname{MEX}(2,4,5,5,0,1)=3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v_6=\\operatorname{MEX}(5,3,0,0,1,3)=2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Therefore, $$$s=\\operatorname{MEX}(0,5,4,1,3,2)=6$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1868A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1868/problem/A"}